// Universe Platform — Shared Database Schema
// Single source of truth for every app (Project Management, CRM, Product
// Database, Tender, Admin) AND every tenant organization using the platform.
// Provider: Azure SQL Database.
//
// MULTI-TENANCY MODEL (added 2026-09-08):
// Universe is a standalone multi-tenant platform, not affiliated with or
// owned by any one customer organization. Every organization that uses it —
// including whichever organization pilots it first — onboards as a fully
// isolated tenant with no special standing over any other. Every domain
// table carries an `organizationId`
// directly (denormalized on purpose, not just reachable via a join) so that:
//   1. The API layer can trivially auto-scope every query to the caller's
//      organization (see apps/api/src/common/tenant-scoped.ts).
//   2. Azure SQL Row-Level Security policies can be applied per-table as a
//      second, independent enforcement layer — so a bug in the API layer
//      alone can't leak one organization's data into another's queries.
// Identity: Microsoft Entra External ID (CIAM), in a dedicated "Universe"
// identity tenant, wholly separate from any customer organization's own
// corporate Entra ID tenant, so no organization's identities mix with
// another's or with Universe's own operating team's directory.
//
// NAMING: "Organization" vs "Partner" (added 2026-09-24 — read this first)
// `Organization` is ALWAYS the tenant root — one row per company using
// Universe as a platform. It is never a client/supplier/manufacturer record.
// A real-world company that a tenant does business with (their client, their
// supplier, their manufacturer, their freight forwarder — any combination of
// these) is a `Partner` instead — a completely different model, scoped to
// the tenant that knows about it via `organizationId`. This mirrors the
// "Organizations + OrganizationRoles" pattern from the 2026-09-24 reference
// architecture review, renamed to `Partner`/`PartnerRole` specifically to
// avoid colliding with the platform's own tenant concept.
//
// HEADER + LINE PROJECTS (added 2026-09-24):
// `Project` is the header (Reference Number, Client, Contact, dates, leads,
// status — facts shared across every item under one engagement). `ProjectLine`
// is one row per item/country/lot, carrying everything that varies per line:
// manufacturer, supplier, pricing, freight, procurement, logistics, and (for
// pharma) batch-level fields. This replaces the earlier 1:1
// ProjectProcurement/ProjectFinancials/ProjectLogistics design, which
// silently assumed one supplier/price/freight arrangement per project — real
// data shows a single Reference Number routinely spans multiple line-level
// facts sharing only the header. See the architecture doc, "Reference
// architecture review (2026-09-24)".
//
// PRODUCT CLASSIFICATION & THE SHARED CATALOG (added 2026-09-24):
// `ProductMaster` is deliberately NOT tenant-scoped — it's shared reference
// data (like the taxonomies below), the same way a dictionary of commodities
// isn't owned by any one user. Individual tenants' own transactional data
// (`ProductLine`, `ProjectLine`) IS tenant-scoped as normal and links to
// `ProductMaster` once a product is identified/matched. This is what makes
// the "type Cryovial, get prompted for size" experience possible, and what
// lets the catalog grow richer as more tenants use the platform — Unimed's
// own already-assigned GS1 GTINs are the first real seed data (owned
// outright, no licensing question), HS codes and the WTO Medical Goods List
// are open and importable now, UNSPSC is free (post-2025 UNDP stewardship)
// pending a signed embedding-terms addendum, and the WHO Essential Medicines
// List (CC BY 3.0 IGO) is safe to use — WHO's Prequalification lists are
// deliberately NOT imported yet pending a written permissions request to
// WHO (see architecture doc, "Sector-insights data strategy").
//
// REFERENTIAL ACTIONS (added 2026-09-10, first real `prisma generate` run):
// Every foreign key below is explicit `onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction`.
// This isn't a stylistic choice — Azure SQL Server rejects a schema where a
// table is reachable from another table's cascade delete/update through more
// than one path, and this schema has many such paths. Rather than hand-tune
// which single path is allowed to cascade (fragile — breaks again the next
// time a relation is added), cascading is turned off everywhere and handled
// explicitly in application code instead. That's arguably the right call
// anyway for a multi-tenant platform: deleting an Organization (or a User, or
// a Project) should be a deliberate, audited service-layer operation, never
// an implicit side effect propagating silently through a dozen tables.
//
// ENUMS (added 2026-09-10, first real `prisma generate` run):
// Prisma does not support native enum types on the SQL Server connector at
// all (a hard platform limitation, confirmed by `prisma generate` itself —
// not a version issue). Every field that was modeled as a Prisma `enum` is a
// `String` column instead; the allowed values are documented in comments
// here and enforced at the application layer. The canonical, importable list
// of these values lives in packages/db/src/enums.ts (@universe/db).

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "sqlserver"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Allowed values reference (enforced in application code, not the database)
// Kept as GLOBAL fixed lists, not per-organization — reinforced 2026-09-24 as
// a hard requirement rather than a "for now" default, since the sector-
// insights goal depends on every tenant using the same values for cross-
// organization comparability.
//
// Project.category         — PROCUREMENT | TECHNICAL_ASSISTANCE
// Project.projectType      — PHARMACEUTICAL | NON_PHARMACEUTICAL
// Project.status           — IDENTIFIED | IN_PROGRESS | SUBMITTED | AWARDED |
//                             COMPLETED | UNAWARDED | DECLINED | CANCELLED
// ProjectLine.incoterm     — EXW | FCA | FAS | FOB | CPT | CIP | CFR | CIF |
//                             DAP | DPU | DDP
// ProjectLine.freightMode  — AIR | SEA | LAND
// ProjectLine.productCategory — CONSUMABLES | DEVICES | REAGENTS | EQUIPMENT |
//                             PHARMACEUTICALS | LABORATORY
// ProjectDocument.type     — CHECKLIST | ISSUES | CLOSEOUT_REPORT | OTHER
// Organization.status      — PILOT | ACTIVE | SUSPENDED
// Organization.type        — BUYER | SUPPLIER (added 2026-09-24 — see
//                             "Supplier/manufacturer marketplace" in the
//                             architecture doc. A SUPPLIER-type org gets the
//                             Supplier Portal app and its own default role
//                             template instead of Project Manager/Read Only.)
// User.platformStaffRole   — NONE | SUPPORT | SUPER_ADMIN
// User.status               — INVITED | ACTIVE | DEACTIVATED
// PartnerRole.roleType      — CLIENT | MANUFACTURER | SUPPLIER |
//                             FREIGHT_FORWARDER | WAREHOUSING | LOGISTICS
// Partner.approvalStatus    — PENDING | APPROVED | REMOVED
// PartnerCertification.type — ISO_13485 | ISO_9001 | ISO_14001 | OTHER_ISO |
//                             FDA_REGISTRATION | GMP | GDP | MIA | WDA | OTHER
// SupplierEnquiry.responseStatus — QUOTED | DECLINED | NO_RESPONSE | WAITING
// ProductMaster.sourceStandard — WHO_EML | HS_CODE | UNSPSC | GS1_GTIN | INTERNAL
// ProductAttributeDefinition.dataType — STRING | NUMBER | BOOLEAN | ENUM
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Organization — the tenant root (see naming note at top of file)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model Organization {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
  name      String
  slug      String   @unique // used in URLs / subdomains
  status    String   @default("PILOT") // see allowed values reference above
  /// BUYER (default) or SUPPLIER — see allowed values reference above and
  /// "Supplier/manufacturer marketplace" in the architecture doc
  /// (2026-09-24). Drives which default role template
  /// createOrganizationWithDefaultRoles gives it and which app(s) it's
  /// steered toward — not an access-control boundary by itself (RLS/role
  /// permissions still do the actual enforcing).
  type      String   @default("BUYER")
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  users            User[]
  roles            Role[]
  partners         Partner[]
  projects         Project[]
  productLines     ProductLine[]
  dataSharingConsents DataSharingConsent[]
  supplierProfile  SupplierProfile?
  supplierProducts SupplierProduct[]
  supplierCountryPresence SupplierCountryPresence[]
  supplierLeadsAsSupplier SupplierLead[] @relation("SupplierLeadSupplier")
  supplierLeadsAsBuyer    SupplierLead[] @relation("SupplierLeadBuyer")

  @@map("organizations")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Identity, roles & permissions (Universe's own app-level RBAC — distinct
// from PartnerRole below, which classifies real-world companies, not users)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// Onboarding is admin-driven, not self-service: a platform-staff member or
/// an org admin creates this row via the Admin app — email, name,
/// organization, and role(s) all set up front, status INVITED, entraObjectId
/// left null. The very first time that email successfully signs in through
/// the Universe CIAM tenant, the auth guard links the verified identity to
/// this row by matching email and flips status to ACTIVE. From that point on
/// the person is recognized by entraObjectId, never by email lookup again.
model User {
  id                String       @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId    String
  organization      Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  entraObjectId     String?      @unique
  email             String       @unique
  forename          String
  surname           String
  jobTitle          String?
  status            String       @default("INVITED") // see allowed values reference above
  platformStaffRole String       @default("NONE")
  invitedById       String?
  invitedBy         User?        @relation("UserInvitedBy", fields: [invitedById], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  invitedUsers      User[]       @relation("UserInvitedBy")
  invitedAt         DateTime     @default(now())
  firstSignInAt     DateTime?
  createdAt         DateTime     @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime     @updatedAt

  projectLeads       ProjectLead[]
  userRoles          UserRole[]
  uploadedDocuments  ProjectDocument[]
  recordedPrices     ProductPriceHistory[]
  acceptedConsents   DataSharingConsent[]
  createdSupplierProducts SupplierProduct[]

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@map("users")
}

/// An app-scoped role BELONGING TO ONE ORGANIZATION. organizationId is
/// nullable only for the small set of platform-level role templates every
/// org can clone from.
model Role {
  id             String        @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String?
  organization   Organization? @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  name           String
  description    String?
  appScope       String
  createdAt      DateTime      @default(now())

  rolePermissions RolePermission[]
  userRoles       UserRole[]

  @@unique([organizationId, name, appScope])
  @@index([organizationId])
  @@map("roles")
}

model Permission {
  id          String  @id @default(uuid())
  key         String  @unique
  description String?

  rolePermissions RolePermission[]

  @@map("permissions")
}

model RolePermission {
  roleId       String
  permissionId String
  role         Role       @relation(fields: [roleId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  permission   Permission @relation(fields: [permissionId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  @@id([roleId, permissionId])
  @@map("role_permissions")
}

model UserRole {
  userId String
  roleId String
  user   User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  role   Role @relation(fields: [roleId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  @@id([userId, roleId])
  @@map("user_roles")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Partners — real-world companies a tenant does business with (2026-09-24,
// replaces the earlier flat Client/Contact model). One row per real company;
// PartnerRole says what role(s) it plays. The same real company (e.g. a
// freight forwarder that's also a warehousing provider) is ONE Partner row
// with multiple PartnerRole entries, not multiple disconnected records.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model Partner {
  id             String       @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String
  organization   Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  name           String
  /// Lowercased, punctuation/legal-suffix-stripped version of `name`, used
  /// for de-duplication and fuzzy matching against messy free-text company
  /// names entered elsewhere (e.g. historical imports).
  normalizedName String
  countryCode    String?      // ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, see Country reference table below
  website        String?
  approvalStatus String       @default("PENDING") // see allowed values reference above
  isArchived     Boolean      @default(false)
  archivedAt     DateTime?
  archivedById   String?
  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())
  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt

  roles            PartnerRole[]
  certifications   PartnerCertification[]
  approvalHistory  PartnerApprovalHistory[]
  supplierDetail   SupplierDetail?
  manufacturerDetail ManufacturerDetail?
  freightForwarderDetail FreightForwarderDetail?
  clientDetail     ClientDetail?
  contacts         Contact[]
  projectsAsClient Project[]              @relation("ProjectClient")
  linesAsManufacturer ProjectLine[]       @relation("LineManufacturer")
  linesAsSupplier  ProjectLine[]          @relation("LineSupplier")
  linesAsFreightForwarder ProjectLine[]   @relation("LineFreightForwarder")
  supplierEnquiries SupplierEnquiry[]
  productLinesAsSupplier ProductLine[]    @relation("ProductLineSupplier")
  productLinesAsManufacturer ProductLine[] @relation("ProductLineManufacturer")

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([organizationId, normalizedName])
  @@map("partners")
}

/// Many-to-many: one Partner can hold several roles at once, each
/// independently active/inactive (e.g. approved as a Supplier, later
/// removed as a Freight Forwarder without touching the Supplier role).
model PartnerRole {
  id        String   @id @default(uuid())
  partnerId String
  partner   Partner  @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  roleType  String   // see allowed values reference above
  isActive  Boolean  @default(true)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@unique([partnerId, roleType])
  @@map("partner_roles")
}

model SupplierDetail {
  partnerId          String  @id
  partner            Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  supplierCode       String?
  productCategory    String? // see allowed values reference above (ProductCategory list)
  fdaRegistrationNumber String?

  @@map("partner_supplier_details")
}

model ManufacturerDetail {
  partnerId         String  @id
  partner           Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  partNumberConvention String?
  countryOfManufactureCode String?

  @@map("partner_manufacturer_details")
}

model FreightForwarderDetail {
  partnerId        String  @id
  partner          Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  preferredIncoterm String? // see allowed values reference above
  serviceRegions   String? @db.NVarChar(Max) // free text for now; structured lanes later

  @@map("partner_freight_forwarder_details")
}

model ClientDetail {
  partnerId       String  @id
  partner         Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  billingAddress  String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  deliveryAddress String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  paymentTerms    String?

  @@map("partner_client_details")
}

/// One generic table for every certificate type, replacing repeated
/// per-certificate column blocks (ISO13485/Expiry/ISO9001/Expiry/...).
model PartnerCertification {
  id         String    @id @default(uuid())
  partnerId  String
  partner    Partner   @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  type       String    // see allowed values reference above
  issuedDate DateTime?
  expiryDate DateTime?
  documentId String?
  document   ProjectDocument? @relation(fields: [documentId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now())

  @@index([partnerId])
  @@index([expiryDate])
  @@map("partner_certifications")
}

/// Audit trail mirroring QA's existing HISTORY sheets: removal/reinstatement
/// events, alongside Partner.approvalStatus for the current state.
model PartnerApprovalHistory {
  id           String    @id @default(uuid())
  partnerId    String
  partner      Partner   @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  action       String    // e.g. "APPROVED" | "REMOVED" | "REINSTATED" — free text for now
  reason       String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  actionDate   DateTime  @default(now())
  actionById   String?

  @@index([partnerId])
  @@map("partner_approval_history")
}

model Contact {
  id             String  @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String // denormalized from Partner for direct RLS scoping
  partnerId      String
  partner        Partner @relation(fields: [partnerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  name           String
  email          String?
  phone          String?
  title          String?

  projectContacts ProjectContact[]

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@map("contacts")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Project — header record (see "HEADER + LINE PROJECTS" note at top of file)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model Project {
  id                       String       @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId           String
  organization             Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  referenceNumber          String
  title                    String
  category                 String // see allowed values reference above
  projectType              String // see allowed values reference above
  clientId                 String?
  client                   Partner?     @relation("ProjectClient", fields: [clientId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Optional, and only ever populated when an organization actually knows
  /// and wants to track it — corrected 2026-09-24: NOT a required structural
  /// concept. A procurement service agent's `client` may or may not be the
  /// actual funder, and is often not knowable to them at all.
  donorReference           String?
  deliveryCountryCode      String? // ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, see Country reference table below
  status                   String       @default("IDENTIFIED") // see allowed values reference above
  startDate                DateTime?
  dueDate                  DateTime?
  submissionDate           DateTime?
  managementResponsibility String?
  reasonForCancellation    String?
  projectNotes             String?      @db.NVarChar(Max)
  projectFolderUrl         String?
  isArchived               Boolean      @default(false)
  archivedAt               DateTime?
  archivedById             String?
  createdAt                DateTime     @default(now())
  updatedAt                DateTime     @updatedAt

  leads     ProjectLead[]
  contacts  ProjectContact[]
  lines     ProjectLine[]
  documents ProjectDocument[]

  // Reference numbers only need to be unique WITHIN an organization — two
  // different tenants can both have a "PROJ-001".
  @@unique([organizationId, referenceNumber])
  @@index([organizationId, status])
  @@index([clientId])
  @@map("projects")
}

/// Which fields are relevant at which Project.status, driving frontend
/// show/hide — added 2026-09-24. The database always keeps every field
/// available regardless of this config, so nothing is lost if a project
/// reopens or skips a phase; this only controls what the UI foregrounds.
model ProjectFieldGroup {
  id           String @id @default(uuid())
  status       String // see allowed values reference above
  fieldGroupKey String // e.g. "core", "submission", "awarded", "completed", "pharma"
  sortOrder    Int    @default(0)

  @@unique([status, fieldGroupKey])
  @@map("project_field_groups")
}

/// Days Remaining for Submission is intentionally NOT stored — it's derived
/// from dueDate/submissionDate and today's date, computed in the API/app
/// layer so it's never stale.

model ProjectLead {
  projectId String
  userId    String
  project   Project @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  user      User    @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  @@id([projectId, userId])
  @@map("project_leads")
}

model ProjectContact {
  projectId String
  contactId String
  project   Project @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  contact   Contact @relation(fields: [contactId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  @@id([projectId, contactId])
  @@map("project_contacts")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ProjectLine — one row per item/country/lot within a Project (2026-09-24,
// replaces the 1:1 ProjectProcurement/ProjectFinancials/ProjectLogistics
// design and absorbs what ProjectLineItem used to hold). Carries procurement,
// financial, and logistics fields generally (not just for pharma), plus the
// pharma-only batch block at the bottom.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model ProjectLine {
  id                            String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId                String // denormalized from Project for direct RLS scoping
  projectId                     String
  project                       Project   @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  // --- Item identification ---
  clientProductDescription      String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  /// Once a product is identified/matched against the shared catalog. Not
  /// required — plenty of lines will never be matched, especially early on.
  productMasterId               String?
  productMaster                 ProductMaster? @relation(fields: [productMasterId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Category-specific refinement attributes (e.g. Cryovial -> size), keyed
  /// by ProductAttributeDefinition.attributeKey, stored as JSON text —
  /// pragmatic middle ground over a full EAV table; validated at the app
  /// layer against the matched product's category definitions.
  attributes                    String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  quantity                      Int?
  productCategory                String?  // see allowed values reference above
  countryOfManufactureCode       String?  // ISO 3166-1 alpha-2

  // --- Procurement ---
  incoterm                      String?   // see allowed values reference above
  freightMode                   String?   // see allowed values reference above
  manufacturerId                String?
  manufacturer                  Partner?  @relation("LineManufacturer", fields: [manufacturerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  supplierId                    String?
  supplier                      Partner?  @relation("LineSupplier", fields: [supplierId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  clientPoNumber                String?
  clientPoReceiptDate           DateTime?
  /// The platform operator's own PO number raised to the supplier.
  internalPoNumber              String?
  internalPoDatePlaced          DateTime?
  /// GAD — confirm exact meaning/definition with Lewis (Goods Arrival Date?)
  gad                           DateTime?
  supplierGad                   DateTime?

  // --- Freight & logistics ---
  freightForwarderId            String?
  freightForwarder               Partner? @relation("LineFreightForwarder", fields: [freightForwarderId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  freightCost                   Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  freightCurrency                String?  @db.Char(3)
  warehouseReferenceNumber      String?
  goodsCollectedDate            DateTime?
  goodsManufacturedDate         DateTime?
  goodsDeliveredToClientDate    DateTime?
  /// Promised/actual date pairs (added 2026-09-24) — replace boolean-only
  /// on-time flags so "days late" can be computed rather than just yes/no,
  /// which is far richer for KPI/benchmarking purposes.
  promisedDeliveryDate          DateTime?
  actualDeliveryDate            DateTime?
  internalOnTime                Boolean?
  supplierOnTime                Boolean?
  supplierInFull                Boolean?

  // --- Financials ---
  supplierUnitPrice             Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  supplierPaymentAmountTotal    Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  supplierPaymentCurrency       String?   @db.Char(3)
  supplierPaymentDate           DateTime?
  supplierDocumentsReceivedDate DateTime?
  supplierPaymentStatusPercent  Decimal?  @db.Decimal(5, 2)
  unitSalesPrice                Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  clientPaymentAmount           Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  clientPaymentCurrency         String?   @db.Char(3)
  clientPaymentDate             DateTime?
  /// The platform operator's own invoice raised to the client.
  internalInvoiceNumber         String?
  internalInvoiceDate           DateTime?
  /// Stored for legacy parity; prefer computing in the API layer so it can't
  /// drift out of sync. Kept override-able since sales may need to adjust.
  grossMargin                   Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  margin                        Decimal?  @db.Decimal(5, 2)

  // --- Pharma-only batch block (shown/required only when
  //     Project.projectType == "PHARMACEUTICAL") ---
  strength                      String?
  form                          String?
  packSize                      String?
  batchNumber                   String?
  expiryDate                    DateTime?
  storageConditions             String?
  dataLoggerReference           String?
  dataLoggerReportReviewed      Boolean?
  excursionReview               String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  customerApproved              Boolean?
  rpApproved                    Boolean?
  /// Marketing Authorization / Product License number
  maPl                          String?

  createdAt                     DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt                     DateTime  @updatedAt

  supplierEnquiries             SupplierEnquiry[]
  priceHistory                  ProductPriceHistory[]

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([projectId])
  @@index([supplierId])
  @@index([manufacturerId])
  @@map("project_lines")
}

/// Turns the RFQ trail that's currently trapped in free-text Notes fields
/// (e.g. "1. Advanced Sterilization Products – No response... 2. Bailey
/// Instruments – declined...") into structured, reportable data.
model SupplierEnquiry {
  id             String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String // denormalized for direct RLS scoping
  projectLineId  String
  projectLine    ProjectLine @relation(fields: [projectLineId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  supplierId     String
  supplier       Partner   @relation(fields: [supplierId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  dateContacted  DateTime?
  responseStatus String    @default("WAITING") // see allowed values reference above
  quotedPrice    Decimal?  @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  quotedCurrency String?   @db.Char(3)
  notes          String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  createdAt      DateTime  @default(now())

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([projectLineId])
  @@map("supplier_enquiries")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Documents (Project Checklist, Project Issues, Project Closeout Report,
// certification documents, etc.)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model ProjectDocument {
  id             String   @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String // denormalized for direct RLS scoping
  projectId      String
  project        Project  @relation(fields: [projectId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  type           String // see allowed values reference above
  title          String
  url            String // blob storage URL or SharePoint link, initially
  uploadedById   String?
  uploadedBy     User?    @relation(fields: [uploadedById], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  uploadedAt     DateTime @default(now())

  partnerCertifications PartnerCertification[]

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@map("project_documents")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Products — three tables at three different grains (2026-09-24), plus the
// shared, non-tenant-scoped ProductMaster catalog. See the note at the top
// of this file, "PRODUCT CLASSIFICATION & THE SHARED CATALOG".
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// PO-line grain — matches the real data's actual grain (one row per
/// purchase order line; the same physical product can appear many times
/// with different POs, suppliers, prices). Tenant-scoped, unlike
/// ProductMaster below.
model ProductLine {
  id                       String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId           String
  organization             Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  customerPoProductName    String
  /// GTIN captured as entered — Unimed's own GS1-assigned codes are expected
  /// to densely populate this from day one (owned data, no licensing
  /// question). Format-validated at the app layer, not pre-populated from
  /// any public catalog (no open bulk GTIN database exists — see
  /// architecture doc, "Sector-insights data strategy").
  gtin                     String?
  poNumber                 String?
  procurementOfficerId     String?
  poDate                   DateTime?
  productType              String?
  supplierId               String?
  supplier                 Partner?  @relation("ProductLineSupplier", fields: [supplierId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  supplierProductDescription String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  manufacturerId           String?
  manufacturer              Partner? @relation("ProductLineManufacturer", fields: [manufacturerId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  manufacturerPartNumber   String?
  unitOfSupply              String?
  exactMatchFlag             Boolean?
  matchNotes                 String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  storageRequirement          String?
  productCertificationExpiry DateTime?
  /// Once matched against the shared catalog.
  productMasterId          String?
  productMaster             ProductMaster? @relation(fields: [productMasterId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt                DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt                DateTime  @updatedAt

  priceHistory              ProductPriceHistory[]

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([gtin])
  @@index([productMasterId])
  @@map("product_lines")
}

/// The shared, deduplicated commodity catalog — NOT tenant-scoped (see note
/// at top of file). Seeded from open reference data (HS codes, the WTO
/// Medical Goods List, UNSPSC once the embedding-terms addendum is signed,
/// the WHO Essential Medicines List) plus Unimed's own owned GTIN data, and
/// grown organically as tenants' real products get matched/added over time.
model ProductMaster {
  id                          String    @id @default(uuid())
  name                        String
  /// Hierarchical category path, e.g. "Laboratory Consumables.Cryovial" —
  /// what ProductAttributeDefinition below is keyed against.
  category                    String
  hsCode                      String?
  unspscCode                  String?
  /// A representative/canonical GTIN where one clearly applies; a given
  /// commodity type may have many manufacturer-specific GTINs in practice —
  /// this is not meant to be exhaustive.
  gtin                        String?
  standardUnit                String?
  canonicalManufacturerPartNumber String?
  expectedQualityDocumentation String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  /// Where this entry's classification data originally came from — an
  /// explicit provenance trail given the mixed licensing landscape across
  /// sources. See allowed values reference above.
  sourceStandard               String?
  isArchived                   Boolean  @default(false)
  createdAt                    DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt                    DateTime @updatedAt

  attributeDefinitions ProductAttributeDefinition[]
  projectLines         ProjectLine[]
  productLines         ProductLine[]
  priceHistory         ProductPriceHistory[]
  supplierProducts     SupplierProduct[]

  @@index([category])
  @@index([hsCode])
  @@index([unspscCode])
  @@index([gtin])
  @@map("product_master")
}

/// Category-scoped refinement field definitions — what powers "type
/// Cryovial, get prompted for size". Not tenant-scoped, same as
/// ProductMaster; defines the schema for the `attributes` JSON on
/// ProjectLine/ProductLine, keyed by category so it applies to every product
/// in that category rather than needing a new database column per type.
model ProductAttributeDefinition {
  id            String  @id @default(uuid())
  category      String
  attributeKey  String
  label         String
  dataType      String  // see allowed values reference above
  /// JSON array of allowed values, only used when dataType == "ENUM".
  enumOptions   String? @db.NVarChar(Max)
  required      Boolean @default(false)
  sortOrder     Int     @default(0)

  productMaster ProductMaster[]

  @@unique([category, attributeKey])
  @@map("product_attribute_definitions")
}

/// Insert-only — pricing is stored and added to, never overwritten, so
/// trend-over-time reporting is a query away. Tenant-scoped (pricing IS
/// commercially sensitive, unlike the shared ProductMaster catalog itself).
model ProductPriceHistory {
  id              String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId  String
  productLineId   String?
  productLine     ProductLine? @relation(fields: [productLineId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  projectLineId   String?
  projectLine     ProjectLine? @relation(fields: [projectLineId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  productMasterId String?
  productMaster   ProductMaster? @relation(fields: [productMasterId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  unitPrice       Decimal   @db.Decimal(18, 2)
  currency        String    @db.Char(3)
  effectiveDate   DateTime  @default(now())
  recordedById    String?
  recordedBy      User?     @relation(fields: [recordedById], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt       DateTime  @default(now())

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([productMasterId])
  @@map("product_price_history")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reference data — Countries & WHO Regions (2026-09-24). Not tenant-scoped.
// Lets country fields (Partner.countryCode, Project.deliveryCountryCode,
// ProjectLine.countryOfManufactureCode) group into the six WHO regions
// (AFRO, AMRO, EMRO, EURO, SEARO, WPRO) — how humanitarian health data is
// normally reported — rather than only raw country-by-country.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

model Region {
  code String    @id // e.g. "AFRO", "AMRO", "EMRO", "EURO", "SEARO", "WPRO"
  name String

  countries Country[]

  @@map("regions")
}

model Country {
  code       String  @id // ISO 3166-1 alpha-2
  name       String
  regionCode String?
  region     Region? @relation(fields: [regionCode], references: [code], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)

  supplierCountryPresence SupplierCountryPresence[]

  @@map("countries")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Data governance — consent for anonymized cross-tenant insights (2026-09-24)
// Schema hook only; the actual consent terms need real legal review before
// any aggregation pipeline is built. See architecture doc, "Sector-insights
// data strategy".
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// One row per organization (organizationId is @unique, not just indexed —
/// see packages/db/src/organizations.ts header comment, added 2026-09-24):
/// consent is contractual, agreed as part of Universe's privacy policy /
/// data sharing agreement at onboarding, not a self-service per-category
/// toggle. createOrganizationWithDefaultRoles() creates this row for every
/// org unconditionally, so "does this org have data-sharing consent" is
/// always `revokedAt IS NULL` on this single row, never "does a row exist".
/// If terms are ever renegotiated for one org, that's `revokedAt` set on
/// this row by platform staff — not a new row (the Insights ETL only ever
/// needs to know the CURRENT state, not history).
model DataSharingConsent {
  id             String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String    @unique
  organization   Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Which data categories this org's agreement covers — JSON array, e.g.
  /// ["pricing","specifications","quality"]. Defaults to
  /// DEFAULT_DATA_SHARING_SCOPE (packages/db/src/organizations.ts) for every
  /// org since the current terms are blanket, not pick-and-choose; kept as a
  /// scoped list (not a boolean) so a future narrower terms version has
  /// somewhere to go without a schema change.
  scope          String    @db.NVarChar(Max)
  termsVersion   String
  acceptedById   String?
  acceptedBy     User?     @relation(fields: [acceptedById], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  acceptedAt     DateTime  @default(now())
  revokedAt      DateTime?

  @@map("data_sharing_consents")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Supplier/manufacturer marketplace (added 2026-09-24 — per Lewis, see
// "Supplier/manufacturer marketplace" in the architecture doc). A SUPPLIER-
// type Organization publishes its own profile, product catalog, and country
// presence, consented and visible to every other organization on the
// platform for search-and-add into their projects — the opposite anonymity
// model from DataSharingConsent's aggregate pool above: here the whole point
// is for suppliers/manufacturers to be identifiable and reachable, in
// exchange for exposure to buyer demand across the platform.
//
// ACCESS MODEL — deliberately NOT the tenant-isolation RLS pattern used
// everywhere else in this file. These three tables need READ access from
// every authenticated user on the platform (that's the product), but WRITE
// access only from the owning supplier organization's own users. See
// infra/sql/supplier-directory-rls.sql for the actual policy — a read-
// everyone / write-owner-only predicate, distinct from
// rls.fn_tenantAccessPredicate's read-and-write-scoped-to-caller's-own-org
// default-deny model. organizationId is still denormalized onto every row
// here for that write-side scoping, consistent with the rest of the schema.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// One row per SUPPLIER-type Organization — its public-facing profile. Not
/// searchable/visible to other organizations until publishedAt is set
/// (lets a supplier complete onboarding before appearing live).
model SupplierProfile {
  id             String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String    @unique
  organization   Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  description    String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  website        String?
  contactName    String?
  contactEmail   String?
  contactPhone   String?
  publishedAt    DateTime?
  createdAt      DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt      DateTime  @updatedAt

  @@map("supplier_profiles")
}

/// Country-level presence — "all levels of specificity" per Lewis, so this
/// is Country- not just Region-grained (Region is always derivable via
/// Country.regionCode when a coarser view is useful). Many rows per org.
model SupplierCountryPresence {
  id             String   @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId String
  organization   Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  countryCode    String
  country        Country  @relation(fields: [countryCode], references: [code], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt      DateTime @default(now())

  @@unique([organizationId, countryCode])
  @@map("supplier_country_presence")
}

/// One row per product a supplier/manufacturer has published to the
/// marketplace. Links to the shared ProductMaster catalog when matched
/// (same mechanism ProductLine/ProjectLine use elsewhere) so a buyer's
/// search-and-add flow can resolve it against the same category taxonomy.
/// Not visible in search until isPublished is true.
model SupplierProduct {
  id                String    @id @default(uuid())
  organizationId    String
  organization      Organization @relation(fields: [organizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  name              String
  description       String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  productMasterId   String?
  productMaster     ProductMaster? @relation(fields: [productMasterId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  /// Category-specific spec values, same JSON-keyed-by-ProductAttributeDefinition
  /// pattern as ProjectLine/ProductLine.attributes — validated at the app
  /// layer against the matched category's definitions.
  specifications    String?   @db.NVarChar(Max)
  gtin              String?
  manufacturerPartNumber String?
  isPublished       Boolean   @default(false)
  createdById       String?
  createdBy         User?     @relation(fields: [createdById], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt         DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt         DateTime  @updatedAt

  @@index([organizationId])
  @@index([productMasterId])
  @@map("supplier_products")
}

/// A lightweight audit trail of buyer interest — created when a buying
/// organization selects a SupplierProduct into one of their own projects
/// (see OrganizationsService's future supplier-directory endpoints). Lets
/// the Supplier Portal show engagement without giving the supplier the
/// buyer's full record — buyerOrganizationId is stored (suppliers should be
/// able to see WHO is interested, that's the point of exposure), but never
/// gives the supplier write/read access into the buyer's own tenant data.
model SupplierLead {
  id                 String   @id @default(uuid())
  supplierOrganizationId String
  supplierOrganization   Organization @relation("SupplierLeadSupplier", fields: [supplierOrganizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  buyerOrganizationId    String
  buyerOrganization      Organization @relation("SupplierLeadBuyer", fields: [buyerOrganizationId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  supplierProductId  String
  supplierProduct    SupplierProduct @relation(fields: [supplierProductId], references: [id], onDelete: NoAction, onUpdate: NoAction)
  createdAt          DateTime @default(now())

  @@index([supplierOrganizationId])
  @@index([buyerOrganizationId])
  @@map("supplier_leads")
}
